--- a/docs/EXECUTOR_PROFILES.md
+++ b/docs/EXECUTOR_PROFILES.md
@@ -220,6 +220,16 @@ Missing cost, duration, token, or model telemetry also remains `unknown`.
 Mission Control must not infer observations from requested values or convert
 missing data to zero.

+Cost telemetry additionally reports `cost_status` as `reported`, `derived`, or
+`unavailable`. `reported` is a runtime's own declared bottom-line dollar figure
+(Claude's `total_cost_usd`). `derived` is a figure Citadel computed by summing
+cost components the runtime itself declared (Claude's per-model `modelUsage`
+breakdown, only when every entry prices cleanly); it is still read only from
+the runtime's own declared output, never estimated from token counts against
+an external price list. `unavailable` covers everything else, including every
+Codex branch today, since Codex's JSONL stream declares tokens but never a
+dollar figure.
+
 Claude model identity comes from the CLI JSON result. Codex exec stdout provides
 the thread ID and token usage but may omit the resolved model. In that case the
 adapter may read only the exact runtime-authored rollout matching the emitted
